@General_member_A — thanks, I’ll escalate with SYNC-4217 and your profile email; if you can also export/send any full app logs from Settings > Help (or paste any additional Sync Log entries) that’ll speed triage, otherwise Support will proceed with the screenshots and timestamps you provided.  
@Enthusiast_member_B — keep Sunrise +30min as your baseline and test it for a week; if winter mornings feel too early try +45–60min or use a morning window (e.g., 6–9 AM) or a geofence-triggered routine so it fires at a sensible local time.  
@Basic_member_C — since you don’t see “Skip,” the simple safe option is Smart Schedules > tap Evening schedule > toggle it OFF now, then toggle it back ON tomorrow (I can walk you through creating a one‑tap Quick Action or calendar reminder if you want).  
@General_member_E — create a new Smart Schedule, select only Saturday and Sunday, set the evening time and actions, give it a unique name (e.g., “Weekend Evening”) and save — it will not overwrite your existing weekday schedule; tell me if you want step‑by‑step taps.

@General_member_A — this was a transient backend issue so no extra action needed now; as a precaution keep the app updated, make sure you tap Save when editing, keep background sync and automatic date/time on, and post the new “Last sync” time here if mismatches recur.  
@Enthusiast_member_B — sunrise +30–45min is a great travel default; when explicit timezone controls roll out, choose the “device/local time” or geofence follow option for true travel behavior, but stick with sunrise if you prefer a natural light-driven trigger.  
@General_member_E — for a Vacation schedule, create it as a separate mode/condition (e.g., Mode = Vacation) and either set your weekend schedule to require Mode = Home or add “only when not Vacation” so Vacation overrides weekend actions; tell me if you want step‑by‑step taps and I’ll post them.

@General_member_A — automatic background sync is usually fine; use "Sync Now" only after lots of rapid edits, before switching devices, or if you see a mismatch, and keep background data & automatic date/time enabled.  
@Enthusiast_member_B — personally I’d keep sunrise+30–45min for a natural feel and switch to a fixed/home-time only if you need strict predictability across zones.  
@General_member_F — check Android system + in‑app notification settings (enable the Automation/Scene channel and set it to High importance), disable battery optimization for the app, confirm DND isn’t blocking, then trigger the scene manually to test; if alerts still drop, clear cache or reinstall and post the Last sync time here.
